### Prerequisites

Before starting the configuration, verify that the following already exist in Business Central:

- the number series to be used for internal contracts, for good codes and for Right of Use fixed assets;
- a depreciation book dedicated to Right of Use fixed assets;
- the chart of accounts, including the accounts to be used for debt, interest and the transitory account;
- the fixed asset classes and subclasses to be assigned to the Right of Use assets;
- the general journal templates and batches to be used for the leasing postings;
- the vendor cards of the leasing companies.

### Configuration

Search for **Leasing Setup (LCM)** and fill in the following fields:

| Field | Description |
|---|---|
| **Fixed Asset Depreciation Book Code** | Depreciation book used for all Right of Use fixed assets created by the module |
| **Good Code No.** | Optional number series for automatically assigning the code of leased goods |
| **Detection over IFRS16 Journ. Templ. Name** / **Detection IFRS16 Batch Name** | General journal template and batch used to post the IFRS16 initial recognition entry |
| **Detection Leasing Journ. Templ. Name** / **Detection Leasing Batch Name** | General journal template and batch used to post the periodic interest detection and debt reduction entries |

If the setup record does not exist yet, it is created automatically the first time the page is opened.

### SGL Integration

If the EOS **Accruals and Simulated General Ledger (SGL)** module is also installed in the environment, the **SGL Integration** section appears on the Leasing Setup (LCM) page, with the fields:

| Field | Description |
|---|---|
| **Enable inheritance from Contract Line to SGL Journal Lines** | If enabled, accrual data is automatically copied from the contract line to the document line when retrieving installments in a purchase invoice |
| **Leasing Accrual Template** | Default accrual template proposed for the interest entries |